<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kurkh Monoliths</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kurkh Monoliths are two Assyrian stelae found in 1861 at Kurkh, near Diyarbakır in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, and now in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-museum">British Museum</a>. One, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shalmaneser-iii">Shalmaneser III</a>, describes his campaigns up to 853 BCE, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qarqar">Battle of Qarqar</a>, and names '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahab">Ahab</a> the Israelite' with 2,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a> and 10,000 foot soldiers. The other records the campaigns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashurnasirpal-ii">Ashurnasirpal II</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kurkh-monoliths.jpg" alt="Kurkh Monoliths" width="173" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yuber · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karkar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
